@lang en

-- us-evidence-of-law.l4 : Title 1, sections 112, 112a(a), 113, 204 and 209 (what Title 1 makes evidence of what).
-- Source: usc01.txt (plain-text rendering, not the official text); quotation lines copy it.
--
-- Each function is named for what its section EXPRESSLY provides: TRUE reads "the section so provides", and FALSE
-- reads "the section does not say so", never "the matter is not evidence". A matter, a publication or a forum that a
-- section does not name is therefore FALSE under that section, and may be evidence under another rule of law.
-- The name of the weight (legal evidence, competent evidence without further proof or authentication, prima facie
-- evidence, conclusive evidence of the original) is part of each function's name, because the four weights are four
-- different things and Title 1 does not rank them.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `us-nouns`
IMPORT `us-interpretation-time`

§ `Chapter 2 and chapter 3 - evidence of the laws`

§§ `Section 112 - Statutes at Large; admissibility in evidence`

-- INERT, section 112 first and second sentences: the Archivist "shall cause to be compiled, edited, indexed, and
-- published" the Statutes at Large with stated contents, and consolidates an extra session into the next regular one.
-- A duty of compilation owed by an office; no fact a downstream encoding asks about turns on it.

-- src:118 | The United States Statutes at Large shall be legal evidence of laws, concurrent resolutions, treaties, international agreements other than treaties, proclamations by the President, and proposed or ratified amendments to the Constitution of the United States therein contained, in all the courts of the United States, the several States, and the Territories and insular possessions of the United States.
@ref 1 U.S.C. s 112, third sentence (src:118)
GIVEN forum IS A `A forum`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 112 names the forum` forum MEANS
    CONSIDER forum
    WHEN `a court of the United States`                                       THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a court of a State`                                                 THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a court of a Territory or insular possession of the United States`  THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE                                                                  FALSE

-- "laws" is read as the two kinds of Act of Congress that section 113 names, a public Act and a private Act (fork F-112-laws).
-- Both proclamation constructors are "proclamations by the President".
@ref 1 U.S.C. s 112, third sentence (src:118)
GIVEN matter IS A `A matter to be proved`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 112 names the matter` matter MEANS
    CONSIDER matter
    WHEN `a public Act of Congress`                                                                          THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a private Act of Congress`                                                                         THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a concurrent resolution`                                                                           THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a treaty`                                                                                          THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an international agreement other than a treaty`                                                    THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a proclamation by the President of a treaty or of an international agreement other than a treaty`  THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a proclamation by the President of some other kind`                                                THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a proposed or ratified amendment to the Constitution of the United States`                         THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE                                                                                                 FALSE

@ref 1 U.S.C. s 112, third sentence (src:118)
GIVEN publication IS A `A publication`
      matter IS A `A matter to be proved`
      `the matter is contained in the publication` IS A BOOLEAN
      forum IS A `A forum`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 112 makes the publication legal evidence of the matter in the forum` publication matter `the matter is contained in the publication` forum MEANS
        publication EQUALS `the United States Statutes at Large`
    AND `section 112 names the matter` matter
    AND `the matter is contained in the publication`
    AND `section 112 names the forum` forum

§§ `Section 112a(a) - United States Treaties and Other International Agreements`

-- INERT, section 112a(a) first sentence: the Secretary of State "shall cause to be compiled, edited, indexed, and
-- published, beginning as of January 1, 1950" the compilation, and says what it contains "during each calendar year".
-- A duty of compilation owed by an office; "calendar year" is a time word Title 1 never defines (see
-- us-interpretation-time.l4, the meaning Title 1 gives to a time word).
-- src:122 | The said United States Treaties and Other International Agreements shall be legal evidence of the treaties, international agreements other than treaties, and proclamations by the President of such treaties and agreements, therein contained, in all the courts of the United States, the several States, and the Territories and insular possessions of the United States.
@ref 1 U.S.C. s 112a(a), second sentence (src:122)
GIVEN matter IS A `A matter to be proved`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 112a(a) names the matter` matter MEANS
    CONSIDER matter
    WHEN `a treaty`                                                                                          THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an international agreement other than a treaty`                                                    THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a proclamation by the President of a treaty or of an international agreement other than a treaty`  THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE                                                                                                 FALSE

@ref 1 U.S.C. s 112a(a), second sentence (src:122)
GIVEN publication IS A `A publication`
      matter IS A `A matter to be proved`
      `the matter is contained in the publication` IS A BOOLEAN
      forum IS A `A forum`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 112a(a) makes the publication legal evidence of the matter in the forum` publication matter `the matter is contained in the publication` forum MEANS
        publication EQUALS `United States Treaties and Other International Agreements`
    AND `section 112a(a) names the matter` matter
    AND `the matter is contained in the publication`
    AND `section 112 names the forum` forum

-- the forum list of section 112a(a) is the same list as section 112's: "in all the courts of the United States, the
-- several States, and the Territories and insular possessions of the United States" (src:118 and src:122).

§§ `Section 113 - "Little and Brown's" edition; slip laws; Treaties and Other International Acts Series`

-- src:201 | The edition of the laws and treaties of the United States, published by Little and Brown, and the publications in slip or pamphlet form of the laws of the United States issued under the authority of the Archivist of the United States, and the Treaties and Other International Acts Series issued under the authority of the Secretary of State shall be competent evidence of the several public and private Acts of Congress, and of the treaties, international agreements other than treaties, and proclamations by the President of such treaties and international agreements other than treaties, as the case may be, therein contained, in all the courts of law and equity and of maritime jurisdiction, and in all the tribunals and public offices of the United States, and of the several States, without any further proof or authentication thereof.
@ref 1 U.S.C. s 113 (src:201)
GIVEN publication IS A `A publication`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 113 names the publication` publication MEANS
    CONSIDER publication
    WHEN `the Little and Brown edition of the laws and treaties`                         THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a slip or pamphlet law issued under the authority of the Archivist`            THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Treaties and Other International Acts Series`                              THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE                                                                             FALSE

@ref 1 U.S.C. s 113 (src:201)
GIVEN matter IS A `A matter to be proved`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 113 names the matter` matter MEANS
    CONSIDER matter
    WHEN `a public Act of Congress`                                                                          THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a private Act of Congress`                                                                         THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a treaty`                                                                                          THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an international agreement other than a treaty`                                                    THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a proclamation by the President of a treaty or of an international agreement other than a treaty`  THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE                                                                                                 FALSE

-- "in all the courts of law and equity and of maritime jurisdiction, and in all the tribunals and public offices of the
-- United States, and of the several States": it names no Territory, insular possession or District of Columbia forum.
@ref 1 U.S.C. s 113 (src:201)
GIVEN forum IS A `A forum`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 113 names the forum` forum MEANS
    CONSIDER forum
    WHEN `a court of the United States`                          THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a court of a State`                                    THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a tribunal or public office of the United States`      THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a tribunal or public office of a State`                THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE                                                     FALSE

-- "as the case may be" is read as: each publication is competent evidence of the matters it contains, which is the
-- input `the matter is contained in the publication` (fork F-113-case).
@ref 1 U.S.C. s 113 (src:201)
GIVEN publication IS A `A publication`
      matter IS A `A matter to be proved`
      `the matter is contained in the publication` IS A BOOLEAN
      forum IS A `A forum`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 113 makes the publication competent evidence of the matter in the forum without any further proof or authentication` publication matter `the matter is contained in the publication` forum MEANS
        `section 113 names the publication` publication
    AND `section 113 names the matter` matter
    AND `the matter is contained in the publication`
    AND `section 113 names the forum` forum

§§ `Section 204 - Codes and Supplements as evidence of the laws; citation`

-- "In all courts, tribunals, and public offices of the United States, at home or abroad, of the District of Columbia, and
-- of each State, Territory, or insular possession of the United States": every forum constructor except one of some other
-- kind. (The text of section 204 says "at home or abroad" of the United States; the forum type has no input for where
-- a tribunal sits, so section 113's unqualified "of the United States" and this one read alike: fork F-abroad.)
-- src:235 | In all courts, tribunals, and public offices of the United States, at home or abroad, of the District of Columbia, and of each State, Territory, or insular possession of the United States—
@ref 1 U.S.C. s 204, introductory words (src:235)
GIVEN forum IS A `A forum`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 204 names the forum` forum MEANS
    NOT (forum EQUALS `a forum of some other kind`)

-- The proviso names a narrower list: "in all the courts of the United States, the several States, and the Territories
-- and insular possessions of the United States" (src:237), which is the list of section 112.
-- src:237 | The matter set forth in the edition of the Code of Laws of the United States current at any time shall, together with the then current supplement, if any, establish prima facie the laws of the United States, general and permanent in their nature, in force on the day preceding the commencement of the session following the last session the legislation of which is included
@ref 1 U.S.C. s 204(a), first limb (src:237)
GIVEN matter IS A `A matter to be proved`
      forum IS A `A forum`
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
      `the day the session following the last session whose legislation is included commences` IS A DATE
      `the title containing the matter has been enacted into positive law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 204(a) makes the Code of Laws and its current supplement prima facie evidence of the law in the forum on the day` matter forum `the day asked about` `the day the session following the last session whose legislation is included commences` `the title containing the matter has been enacted into positive law` MEANS
        matter EQUALS `a law of the United States, general and permanent in its nature`
    AND `section 204 names the forum` forum
    AND `the day asked about` EQUALS `the day as at which a Code establishes the law` `the day the session following the last session whose legislation is included commences`
    AND NOT `the title containing the matter has been enacted into positive law`

-- src:237 | Provided, however, That whenever titles of such Code shall have been enacted into positive law the text thereof shall be legal evidence of the laws therein contained, in all the courts of the United States, the several States, and the Territories and insular possessions of the United States
@ref 1 U.S.C. s 204(a), the proviso (src:237)
GIVEN `the title containing the matter has been enacted into positive law` IS A BOOLEAN
      forum IS A `A forum`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 204(a) makes the text of a title enacted into positive law legal evidence of the laws it contains in the forum` `the title containing the matter has been enacted into positive law` forum MEANS
        `the title containing the matter has been enacted into positive law`
    AND `section 112 names the forum` forum

-- 204(b): the District of Columbia list excludes "such laws as are of application in the District of Columbia by reason
-- of being laws of the United States general and permanent in their nature".
-- src:239 | The matter set forth in the edition of the Code of the District of Columbia current at any time shall, together with the then current supplement, if any, establish prima facie the laws, general and permanent in their nature, relating to or in force in the District of Columbia on the day preceding the commencement of the session following the last session the legislation of which is included, except such laws as are of application in the District of Columbia by reason of being laws of the United States general and permanent in their nature.
@ref 1 U.S.C. s 204(b) (src:239)
GIVEN matter IS A `A matter to be proved`
      `it applies in the District of Columbia only by reason of being a law of the United States general and permanent in its nature` IS A BOOLEAN
      forum IS A `A forum`
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
      `the day the session following the last session whose legislation is included commences` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 204(b) makes the Code of the District of Columbia and its current supplement prima facie evidence of the law in the forum on the day` matter `it applies in the District of Columbia only by reason of being a law of the United States general and permanent in its nature` forum `the day asked about` `the day the session following the last session whose legislation is included commences` MEANS
        matter EQUALS `a law relating to or in force in the District of Columbia, general and permanent in its nature`
    AND NOT `it applies in the District of Columbia only by reason of being a law of the United States general and permanent in its nature`
    AND `section 204 names the forum` forum
    AND `the day asked about` EQUALS `the day as at which a Code establishes the law` `the day the session following the last session whose legislation is included commences`

-- 204(c) to (e): the forms in which a Code, a supplement and a new edition "may be cited". "May" permits; it does not
-- require. A citation in some other form is therefore not forbidden by these subsections, only not provided for by them.
-- src:241 | The Code of the District of Columbia may be cited as “D.C. Code”.
@ref 1 U.S.C. s 204(c) (src:241)
GIVEN citation IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 204(c) permits this citation of the Code of the District of Columbia` citation MEANS
    citation EQUALS "D.C. Code"

-- Roman figures: the text says "Roman figures denoting the number of the supplement" and gives no numeral rules.
-- The subtractive convention (IV, IX, XL, XC, CD, CM) is taken (fork F-roman), and the largest figure written is
-- MMMCMXCIX (3999), after which the text gives no figure. This is the one helper in the module that is not a section.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A STRING
`the Roman figures for the remainder` n MEANS
    BRANCH IF n AT LEAST 1000 THEN CONCAT "M",  `the Roman figures for the remainder` (n MINUS 1000)
           IF n AT LEAST 900  THEN CONCAT "CM", `the Roman figures for the remainder` (n MINUS 900)
           IF n AT LEAST 500  THEN CONCAT "D",  `the Roman figures for the remainder` (n MINUS 500)
           IF n AT LEAST 400  THEN CONCAT "CD", `the Roman figures for the remainder` (n MINUS 400)
           IF n AT LEAST 100  THEN CONCAT "C",  `the Roman figures for the remainder` (n MINUS 100)
           IF n AT LEAST 90   THEN CONCAT "XC", `the Roman figures for the remainder` (n MINUS 90)
           IF n AT LEAST 50   THEN CONCAT "L",  `the Roman figures for the remainder` (n MINUS 50)
           IF n AT LEAST 40   THEN CONCAT "XL", `the Roman figures for the remainder` (n MINUS 40)
           IF n AT LEAST 10   THEN CONCAT "X",  `the Roman figures for the remainder` (n MINUS 10)
           IF n AT LEAST 9    THEN CONCAT "IX", `the Roman figures for the remainder` (n MINUS 9)
           IF n AT LEAST 5    THEN CONCAT "V",  `the Roman figures for the remainder` (n MINUS 5)
           IF n AT LEAST 4    THEN CONCAT "IV", `the Roman figures for the remainder` (n MINUS 4)
           IF n AT LEAST 1    THEN CONCAT "I",  `the Roman figures for the remainder` (n MINUS 1)
           OTHERWISE ""

GIVETH A STRING
`Title 1 gives no Roman figure for a number that is not a whole number from 1 to 3999` MEANS
    REFUSE "Title 1 gives no Roman figure for a number that is not a whole number from 1 to 3999"

-- src:243 | Supplements to the Code of Laws of the United States and to the Code of the District of Columbia may be cited, respectively, as “U.S.C., Sup. ”, and “D.C. Code, Sup. ”, the blank in each case being filled with Roman figures denoting the number of the supplement.
@ref 1 U.S.C. s 204(d) (src:243)
GIVEN `the number of the supplement` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A STRING
`the Roman figures denoting the number of the supplement` `the number of the supplement` MEANS
    IF     `the number of the supplement` AT LEAST 1
       AND `the number of the supplement` AT MOST 3999
       AND TRUNC `the number of the supplement` 0 EQUALS `the number of the supplement`
    THEN `the Roman figures for the remainder` `the number of the supplement`
    ELSE `Title 1 gives no Roman figure for a number that is not a whole number from 1 to 3999`

-- The blank is "filled with Roman figures". The quotation marks print the blank as a space after the stop: `Sup. `.
@ref 1 U.S.C. s 204(d) (src:243)
GIVEN `the number of the supplement` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A STRING
`the citation section 204(d) permits for a supplement to the Code of Laws of the United States` `the number of the supplement` MEANS
    CONCAT "U.S.C., Sup. ", `the Roman figures denoting the number of the supplement` `the number of the supplement`

@ref 1 U.S.C. s 204(d) (src:243)
GIVEN `the number of the supplement` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A STRING
`the citation section 204(d) permits for a supplement to the Code of the District of Columbia` `the number of the supplement` MEANS
    CONCAT "D.C. Code, Sup. ", `the Roman figures denoting the number of the supplement` `the number of the supplement`

-- src:245 | New editions of each of such codes may be cited, respectively, as “U.S.C., ed.”, and “D.C. Code, ed.”, the blank in each case being filled with figures denoting the last year the legislation of which is included in whole or in part.
@ref 1 U.S.C. s 204(e) (src:245)
GIVEN `the last year the legislation of which is included in whole or in part` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A STRING
`the citation section 204(e) permits for a new edition of the Code of Laws of the United States` `the last year the legislation of which is included in whole or in part` MEANS
    CONCAT "U.S.C., ed. ", TOSTRING `the last year the legislation of which is included in whole or in part`

@ref 1 U.S.C. s 204(e) (src:245)
GIVEN `the last year the legislation of which is included in whole or in part` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A STRING
`the citation section 204(e) permits for a new edition of the Code of the District of Columbia` `the last year the legislation of which is included in whole or in part` MEANS
    CONCAT "D.C. Code, ed. ", TOSTRING `the last year the legislation of which is included in whole or in part`

§§ `Section 209 - Copies of Supplements; conclusive evidence of original`

-- src:265 | Copies of the Code of Laws relating to the District of Columbia and copies of the supplements provided for by sections 202 and 203 of this title printed at the Government Publishing Office and bearing its imprint, shall be conclusive evidence of the original of such code and supplements in the custody of the Administrator of General Services.
@ref 1 U.S.C. s 209 (src:265)
GIVEN copy IS A `A printed copy`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 209 makes the copy conclusive evidence of the original in the custody of the Administrator of General Services` copy MEANS
        (   copy's `it is a copy of the Code of Laws relating to the District of Columbia`
         OR copy's `it is a copy of a supplement provided for by section 202 or section 203`)
    AND copy's `it was printed at the Government Publishing Office`
    AND copy's `it bears the imprint of the Government Publishing Office`
